WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.100
Autumn in Amritsar.

2
00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:06.280
The Golden Temple is lit with
lamps, candles and lights,

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.350
and fireworks burst.

4
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.050
Sikhs are remembering a release
from a prison fort, long ago.

5
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.120
Now spring, at Anandpur, in 1699.

6
00:00:17.170 --> 00:00:18.750
A crowd has gathered.

7
00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.040
A voice asks: who will give his head?

8
00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:25.040
Why would Sikhs still
celebrate a prison release,

9
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.100
and a call for a head?

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.340
In this mission, you'll follow
what happened at Anandpur,

11
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.190
and see how Sikhs mark the
festival of Vaisakhi today.

12
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.740
Then you'll trace a journey
from a prison fort to Amritsar,

13
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:40.490
and find out why it still matters.

14
00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.440
Your mission: find out why Sikhs light
up a temple for a prisoner's release,

15
00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:47.570
and remember a call for a head.
